WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:09.929
May it be the era of Kings and Queens, or
may it be today’s modern world….

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:14.760
Silk has always been the choice of several
people for all the wonderful qualities

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.680
it has!

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.660
Since ancient times, textile industry has
been ruled by silk!

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:25.910
However, being in demand does NOT mean it
is easily available and is

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.520
economically viable!

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.890
Yes, it’s not easily available, and is expensive!

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.230
This has made people search for alternatives!

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.140
And finally the search was
concluded when an artificial fibre resembling

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.739
silk was synthesised.

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:47.969
Wait a second…Does that mean we find synthetic
fibre which is like silk?

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.110
Of
course yes!

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.110
And what do we call it?

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.770
It is known as RAYON!

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:55.590
Have we come across this fibre?

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.289
Of course yes!

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:00.320
It has got several daily life
applications.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.739
From the fabric we use to make various outfits,
to the bed sheets

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:07.969
used by us… it is used in many applications!

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:12.490
But if we say that it is synthetic and at
the same time has appearance of silk,

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:14.950
then how exactly is it made?

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.219
Let us know this first.

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:21.479
It was in the end of nineteenth century that
silk availability was a concern due

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:23.270
to its extremely high cost.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:29.619
As a result many chemists began finding an
alternative to it.

00:01:29.619 --> 00:01:33.789
Finally after many successful attempts to
make something close to silk, a type

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:36.119
of rayon got introduced in France.

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:43.399
In around 1889 a French industrialist named
Hilaire de Chardonnet introduced the “CHARDONNET

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:47.810
SILK” which was the first
ever man made rayon manufactured at industrial

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.500
scale.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.909
Since then many varieties have got introduced
that have the appearance of silk

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:56.319
but are actually Rayon!

00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:59.630
But how do we exactly make such a beautiful
fibre?

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.310
The commencing material
is CELLULOSE.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:06.849
Wait a second….cellulose is what we find
in plants right?

00:02:06.849 --> 00:02:07.969
Yes!

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:12.240
Usually wooden pulp is used as a source of
cellulose.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.650
This is converted
into soluble compound that is further pressed

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.790
with force through an
instrument having fine holes.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.700
What will be the result of this?

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:22.700
Yes!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.659
Thin fibres
will be formed.

00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:28.371
These are further treated with chemicals and
at the end, rayon

00:02:28.371 --> 00:02:29.709
fibres are obtained.

00:02:29.709 --> 00:02:35.099
Now you may wonder that even if we process
it, the starting material still

00:02:35.099 --> 00:02:36.819
remains natural!

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:40.490
The starting material I’m talking about
is cellulose.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.599
So how
can we say that it is synthetic?

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:45.180
You are on the correct track!

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:51.069
This is exactly why
Rayon is not considered to be entirely synthetic!

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:53.489
In fact Rayon is known to be
Semi-synthetic.

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:58.079
That is partly natural and partly synthetic!

00:02:58.079 --> 00:03:02.890
Now we have been talking about this ARTIFICIAL
SILK for quite some time.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.290
Can
you tell me where exactly we use it?

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.440
The major use of Rayon is in making clothes!

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.510
Yes!

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.099
Rayon can be blended with
many dyes to get vibrant shades, which is

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:17.739
why it is widely used in the textile
industry.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:21.829
Not only clothing, but it can also be used
in making bed sheets when mixed

00:03:21.829 --> 00:03:23.860
with natural fibres like Cotton.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:28.749
Can we mix it with any other natural fibre
as well?

00:03:28.749 --> 00:03:29.749
Yes!

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:32.060
Rayon can also be
blended with wool.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.430
This helps us get soft, shiny fibre that can
be used to make

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.019
carpets!

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:41.329
Now you may be wondering if we can use rayon
to make some tough material

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:43.319
that has great strength…

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:48.069
Well, tensile strength is not the property
of Rayon.

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:49.069
In

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:52.280
fact it is best exhibited by the fibre Nylon.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.440
But to study it, you will have to
watch our next video!

